e threw two touchdown passes and ran for a score to lead Connecticut to a 35-16 victory over Massachusetts on Friday night.","story":"EAST HARTFORD, Conn. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079619/kalieb-osborne\" target=\"_new\">Kalieb Osborne</a> threw two touchdown passes and ran for a score to lead Connecticut to a 35-16 victory over Massachusetts on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870959/shamar-porter\" target=\"_new\">Shamar Porter</a> had a first-quarter touchdown catch for UConn (4-3), then <a href=\"https://x.com/UConnFootball/status/2113803407635202533?s=20\">blocked a punt</a> and recovered it in the end zone for a 28-3 advantage in the third.\n\n\r\n              Osborne completed 14 of 19 passes for 173 yards. He capped the Huskies' scoring on a 13-yard run with 3:04 left to play.\n\n\r\n              UMass (4-4) grabbed the lead when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5218751/derek-morris\" target=\"_new\">Derek Morris</a> kicked a 24-yard field goal at the end of a game-opening 13-play drive that lasted nearly eight minutes. \n\n\r\n              Osborne threw a 5-yard touchdown pass to Porter on third-and-goal and UConn used 13 plays on its first possession to take a lead it never relinquished.\n\n\r\n              Osborne connected with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5125750/jd-willoughby\" target=\"_new\">JD Willoughby</a> for a 20-yard touchdown with 1:36 remaining in the second quarter, and Cyncir <a href=\"https://x.com/UConnFootball/status/2113788481231065356?s=20\">Bowers added</a> a 70-yard touchdown run 32 seconds later — after a fifth straight three-and-out by the Minutemen — for a 21-3 lead at halftime.\n\n\r\n              William “Pop” Watson III threw a short touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388331/curtis-kimmons-iv\" target=\"_new\">Curtis Kimmons IV</a> in the fourth quarter for UMass, which has lost four in a row. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/3949937/justin-williams\" target=\"_new\">Justin Williams</a>-Thomas added a 6-yard touchdown run.\n\n\r\n              Bowers rushed 15 times for 131 yards to help UConn take a 39-38-2 lead over UMass in a series that began in 1897.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              UMass: Hosts Ball State on Nov. 4.\n\n\r\n              UConn: At Air Force on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-24T02:51:51Z"}}